    translit: "Varaṃ parvatadurgeṣu bhrāntaṃ vanacaraiḥ saha |\nNa mūrkhajanasamparkaḥ surendrabhavaneṣvapi ||",
    meaningEn: "Better to wander in mountain fortresses with forest dwellers than to associate with fools even in the palaces of Indra.",
