    translit: "Manasi vacasi kāye puṇyapīyūṣapūrṇāḥ\nTribhuvanamupakāraśreṇibhiḥ prīṇayantaḥ |\nParaguṇaparamāṇūn parvatīkṛtya nityaṃ\nNijahṛdi vikasantaḥ santi santaḥ kiyantaḥ ||",
    meaningEn: "How rare are those noble souls who are filled with the nectar of virtue in thought, word, and deed; who delight the three worlds through continuous acts of service; who magnify even the smallest virtues of others into mountains; and who always bloom from within their own hearts.",
    explanationEn: "A verse of rare tenderness from Bhartuhari. Against the sharp satire of many Nītiśataka verses, this one pauses to appreciate the genuinely good person. Three qualities define them: integration of thought, word, and action; a habit of service; and the generous magnification of others' goodness. The question \"how rare are they?\" is both a lament and a call — such people exist, but they are precious, and worth cultivating.",
    meaningMr: "मन, वाणी आणि कर्म — तिन्हींमध्ये पुण्याचा अमृतरस भरलेले; तीन लोकांना सेवेने आनंदित करणारे; दुसऱ्याच्या छोट्याशा गुणाला डोंगराएवढे मानणारे; आणि स्वतःच्या हृदयात सदा फुलत राहणारे — असे सज्जन किती असतात?",
    explanationMr: "भर्तृहरि इथे थांबतो आणि विचारतो — खरोखर चांगलं माणूस किती असतं? हे प्रश्न म्हणजे एक सौम्य खंत आणि एक सुंदर आदर्श. विचार-वाणी-कर्म एकसारखं असणं, दुसऱ्याचे गुण मोठे करणं, सतत सेवाभावी राहणं — हे दुर्मीळ आहे. पण ते शोधायला हवं, आणि स्वतःत जोपासायला हवं.",
    source: "Nītiśataka, verse 77",
