    translit: "Prasahya maṇimuddharen makara vaktra daṃṣṭrāntarāt\nSamudramapi santaret pracaladūrmimālākulam |\nBhujaṅgamapi kopitaṃ śirasi puṣpavaddhārayet\nNa tu pratiniviṣṭamūrkhajanacittamārādhayet ||",
    meaningEn: "One may forcibly extract a jewel from between a crocodile's fangs; one may cross a turbulent ocean of surging waves; one may even wear an enraged serpent on one's head like a garland of flowers — but one cannot satisfy the mind of a stubborn fool.",
