    translit: "Bhogā na bhuktā vayameva bhuktāḥ\nTapo na taptaṃ vayameva taptāḥ |\nKālo na yāto vayameva yātāḥ\nTṛṣṇā na jīrṇā vayameva jīrṇāḥ ||",
    meaningEn: "Pleasures were not enjoyed — we ourselves were consumed. Austerity was not practised — we ourselves were scorched by it. Time did not pass — we ourselves passed away. Desire did not age — we ourselves aged.",
