    translit: "Ambho dhātri tṛṣā me manasi capalitā śeṣatā yāvad asti\nTāvad brahmāmṛtāya sphurati rasanayā meghavad vāk pravāhaḥ |\nŚrotrotkaṇṭhā muhurmuhurapi ca manasaḥ satvatā bhāvanābhyāṃ\nTṛṣṇāvyāpāramokṣāya sakalam akhilaṃ jīvitaṃ me prayātu ||",
    meaningEn: "O earth, as long as I have this thirst in my restless mind, may the flood of speech flow from my tongue like clouds for the nectar of Brahman; may the ears yearn again and again through the sattva of contemplation — and may my entire life go toward the liberation from the activity of desire.",
