    translit: "Ārambhagurvī kṣayiṇī krameṇa laghvī purā vṛddhimatī ca paścāt |\nDinasya pūrvārdhaparārdhabhinnā chāyeva maitrī khalasajjanānām ||",
    meaningEn: "The friendship of the wicked is great at the start and gradually diminishes; the friendship of the good is small at first and grows larger with time — like the shadow of the first and second halves of the day.",
