    meaningEn: "Water on a red-hot iron plate is not even heard by name — it vanishes. The same water, falling on a lotus petal, shines like a pearl. Falling into the oyster shell under the Svāti star, it becomes a true pearl. A person's quality is mostly determined by the company they keep.",
