    translit: "Atyantakopaḥ kaṭuvaktā daridratā\nPravāsī bhāryā bandhuhīnatā |\nĀdhikyamātmanyapi bhoginaḥ khalu\nVṛthā nṛṇāmāyurudāharanti ṣaṭ ||",
    meaningEn: "Excessive anger; harsh speech; poverty; a husband who is always travelling; having no relatives; and excessive self-indulgence — these six, they say, waste human life pointlessly.",
