    translit: "Iyam hi sarvaśāstrāṇāṃ puṇyādreḥ pariṇāmajam |\nRasāyanamiva proktaṃ śamasaukhyapradāyakam ||\nVairāgyamabhidhāsyāmi saṃsārabhayabhīruṇām |\nSādhūnāmupakārāya na svārthāya mayocyate ||",
    meaningEn: "This teaching, born as the finest essence of all scriptures from the sacred mountain of wisdom, is declared like a rasāyana — a medicine of peace and happiness. I speak of vairāgya for those who are afraid of the suffering of worldly existence. This is spoken for the benefit of the good — not for my own purpose.",
