    translit: "Sā ramyā nagarī mahān sa nṛpatiḥ sāmantacakraṃ ca tat\nPārśve tasya ca sā vidagdhaparīṣat tāśca tatkālakaṭhāḥ |\nTadvattacca śṛṇoti dūrataratah khedena sāśruplāvaiḥ\nNaṣṭaṃ taddhi śarīramadya vilasad daivāt kimanyad vadet ||",
    meaningEn: "That beautiful city, that great king, that circle of feudatory lords; beside him, that assembly of clever courtiers, those stories of those times — hearing of all this from so far away with grief and tear-filled eyes, that very body which once shone in it all is now lost. What else can one say but — fate?",
