    translit: "Yanmāyāvibhrameṇa bhramati bhuvi jano mohito mohadoṣaiḥ |\nYat sarvaṃ brahmamayaṃ jagaditi paricintyadya bodhaṃ prayāhi |\nYasmādviśvaṃ samutthaṃ tadabhilaṣati yatsarvamevāntarāste |\nTat brahmāvehi tanmāṃ viditamakhilamityeva vijñānamāhuḥ ||",
    meaningEn: "People wander on earth, deluded by the illusion of māyā, afflicted by the fault of delusion. Reflecting that the entire world is Brahman, go now to awakening. From which the universe arises, which all things desire, which dwells within everything — know that as Brahman; knowing that, all is known. This alone is called true knowledge.",
