    translit: "Ekākī niḥspṛhaḥ śāntaḥ pāṇipātro digambaraḥ |\nKadā śāntamanāḥ śaile ramiṣyāmi nirāmayaḥ ||",
    meaningEn: "Alone, desireless, peaceful, with the hand as begging bowl, sky-clad — when will I, with a quiet mind, take delight in the mountain, free from all disease?",
