    translit: "Tāvad bhayasya bhetavyaṃ yāvadbhayamanāgatam |\nĀgataṃ tu bhayaṃ dṛṣṭvā prahartavyamabhītavat ||",
    meaningEn: "Fear should be feared only as long as it has not arrived. But when fear has come and is seen — strike it without flinching, as the fearless do.",
