    translit: "Panthānaṃ te gantumicchāmi dūraṃ\ntatra sthitvā tvatprasādena devi |\nŚāntiṃ yāsyāmi kimiti vadet pathikastvat-samāgame\nvasan puṇyastvāmeva gāyatīti ||",
    meaningEn: "\"I wish to travel your road, O Goddess, far away — dwelling there by your grace, I will attain peace.\" What would the traveller say upon meeting you? The virtuous one dwelling in your company sings only of you.",
